<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47842" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμβ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, also ὁ
		<i><span class="en">
			Simon.
			237
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>Ec.</u>
			12.5
		</span></i> (pl.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέθηπα</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>amazement</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δ᾽ ἔχεν εἰσορόωντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.79
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δ᾽ ἕλε πάντας ἰδόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.372
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμβει δυσφόρῳ τερπνῷ τε μιχθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					1.55
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμβει ἐκπλαγέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					291
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				781
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				254c
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				41.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in objective
			sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμβοι</span>
			<i>terrors</i> in the way, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> l.c.; <i>object of wonder,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epigr.Gr.
				1068
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Gerasa</span>).</div>
